# Learning Hub — design & SEO

Before changing **layout, typography, colors, or page structure**, read **`DESIGN.md`** in the repo root and follow it.

## Must follow

- **Visual**: Gen Z–adjacent = **minimal, scannable, one accent** (`--accent` in `DESIGN.md`); generous spacing; no decorative clutter. Support **light + dark** via `prefers-color-scheme` and tokens.
- **Typography**: body **≥16px**, comfortable line-height, **max-width ~65–75ch** for long prose.
- **SEO HTML**: **one `h1` per page**; logical `h2` → `h3`; use **`main`**, **`nav`**, **`article`** when appropriate; **`lang`** on `<html>` matches route.
- **Astro**: in JSX-style tags use **`hrefLang`** on `<link>` (not `hreflang`); avoid **nested backticks** inside `{expression}` in templates — compute URLs in frontmatter.
- **Links & a11y**: visible **`:focus-visible`**; meaningful **`alt`** on images.

## Do not

- Generic “AI slop” (purple gradients, random blobs) unless specified.
- Fake headings (`<p>` styled as titles).
- Body text smaller than ~14px on mobile for primary content.

When in doubt, align new pages with **`src/pages/[lang]/index.astro`** patterns and tokens until a shared `global.css` exists.
